# SagaTree

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) before changing code.

## Stack

- React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind + Radix
- Node/Hono host — Better Auth, Policy Service, SQLite, local assets (`server/`)
- Optional AI/Media providers (Ollama/BYOK, LiveKit, Meshy); core runs without them
- Legacy Supabase/Edge archived under `archive/supabase-legacy/` (not product)
- UI/errors Deutsch; commits and PR text English
- Quality gate: `npm run test-gate` (includes architecture-boundary-check)

## Architecture (#94)

- `src/domains/**` — pure business/rules (no React, no Host/ORM/HTTP SDKs)
- `src/infrastructure/**` — Host HTTP / network adapters only
- `src/app/<domain>/<slice>/` — vertical user journeys
- `src/modules/**` / `src/components/**` eradicated — do not recreate
- Character: `edit/` is composition root; consume `creation/` + `progression/` via public barrels only

## Workflow

- Issue branches from `main` — never commit directly to `main`
- Acceptance: `.qa/acceptance/<slug>.md` when present
- Composition proof: `.qa/runs/composition-gate-<slug>.md` (CLEAR/SKIPPED for current HEAD)
- Ship only after `@ecc-check` READY / green CI **and** Kodus (`Kody Code Review` Complete on HEAD) + Codex findings cleared — see AGENTS.md “External AI Review Contract”
- Long queues: after each merge, update handoff + auto-compact in-session, then immediately next issue — see AGENTS.md “Context compact & long queues”

## Security

- Owner-scoped data stays owner-scoped (Policy Service + service checks)
- Client writes must not invent elevated origins or cross-owner FKs
- Security reviews list **all** severities including Low/Info
